review_comment:
I think this test will fail to notice if there are too many samples with the given `key`, because as soon as the count hits zero, the entry is removed, and thereafter, we do no more checks. The existing logic also had this bug.

Also, style-wise, this could use `map.computeIfPresent` if you find that cleaner at all:

```
histogramAssertions.computeIfPresent(key, (k, old) -> {
    int counts = WHATEVER;
    var remaining = old - counts;
    if (remaining == 0) {
        return null;
    } else {
        return remaining;
    }
});
```

